1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,720
Next time you see a pigeon flying around, look at it with some respect - it might be able to help with the diagnosis and treatment of human diseases.
下次当你看到一只鸽子四处飞翔时，要带着几分敬意看待它——它或许能够帮助对人类疾病进行诊断和治疗。

2
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:18,030
A recent study has shown that these birds could be trained to detect breast cancer from images as accurately as humans.
最近的一项研究表明，这些鸽子可以经过训练，像人类一样准确地从图像中检测出乳腺癌。

3
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:24,760
It's all about their visual memory - these birds have plenty of it even if their brains are very small.
这一切都归功于它们的视觉记忆——尽管这些鸽子的大脑非常小，但它们却拥有强大的视觉记忆能力。

4
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:43,370
Professor Edward Wasserman from the University of Iowa, a co-author of the study, says: "Pigeons can distinguish identities and emotional expressions on human faces, letters of the alphabet, misshapen pharmaceutical capsules, and even paintings by Monet versus Picasso."
爱荷华大学的爱德华·沃瑟曼教授是这项研究的合著者之一，他说：“鸽子能够区分人类面部的个性特征和情感表达、字母表中的字母、形状不规则的药品胶囊，甚至还能区分莫奈和毕加索的画作。”

5
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:53,250
And Wasserman adds that the birds' visual memory capacity is equally impressive, with a proven recall of more than 1,800 images.
沃瑟曼还补充说，鸽子的视觉记忆能力同样令人印象深刻，经证实它们能够回想起超过1800张图像。

6
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:58,330
So how did the scientists find out about the amazing ability of these birds?
那么科学家们是如何发现这些鸽子的惊人能力的呢？

7
00:00:58,330 --> 00:01:08,380
They taught different pigeons to distinguish microscope images of cancerous and non-cancerous tissue and rewarded them with food every time they got it right.
他们训练不同的鸽子区分显微镜下癌变的和非癌变的组织图像，并且每次鸽子判断正确时，就给它们食物作为奖励。

8
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:10,640
It didn't take long to get good results.
没过多久就取得了良好的效果。

9
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:22,760
After two weeks of training in 'pigeon medical school', the 'students' recorded 85% accuracy as they managed to identify cancerous tissue from images they had not seen before.
在“鸽子医学院”接受了两周的训练后，这些“学生”能够从它们从未见过的图像中识别出癌变组织，准确率达到了85%。

10
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:28,110
But pigeons are not the only animals showing potential to help human diagnosis.
但鸽子并不是唯一有潜力帮助人类进行诊断的动物。

11
00:01:28,110 --> 00:01:38,010
A team at the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences has shown that a dog can be trained to smell urine samples of patients to identify thyroid cancer.
阿肯色大学医学科学团队已经证明，狗可以经过训练嗅闻患者的尿液样本，以识别甲状腺癌。

12
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:42,150
It lay down when it could smell cancer and turned away if not.
当它能嗅出癌症时就会趴下，如果没有检测到癌症则会转身离开。

13
00:01:42,150 --> 00:01:45,800
The animals got it right in 30 cases out of 34.
在34个案例中，这些狗正确判断了30个。

14
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:49,010
So don't dismiss the abilities of these animals.
所以不要轻视这些动物的能力。

15
00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:51,760
They might be much more intelligent than you think.
它们可能比你想象的要聪明得多。
